{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Ce4maccLpWkh3vnzrhtDZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I would add the new rule to section 2, immediately after the existing second bullet point:\n\n```markdown\n## 2. Flag lifecycle\n\n- **No flag outlives its purpose.** Each flag exists from the change\n  that introduces it until the day no path in the source can still\n  reach it; the steward listed with it carries it over that whole\n  span.\n- **Rollout figures are stated, never inherited.** No flag takes a\n  default exposure; the flag sheet states the percentage and the\n  cohort it applies to.\n- **A flag is deleted once the rollout has stood at 100% for a full\n  release, not merely marked done** — one left behind keeps both\n  branches running. Record the clearing release beside the figure.\n```\n\nThis placement belongs in the lifecycle section because it specifies the concrete end-state condition and removal procedure for flags, which is a natural continuation of the \"no flag outlives its purpose\" principle already stated there, and it directly complements the rule about stated rollout figures by explaining what happens when a rollout reaches completion."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":240,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
